biguity"}], "description": "Students connect these techniques to expanded tonal palettes."}]}, {"id": "faea0044-0169-4f7f-b3e0-1ddda504b3b2", "type": "topic", "title": "Chromatic Harmony in Context", "description": "Students synthesize chromatic harmony through repertoire, listening, and stylistic interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "030aae08-94e2-468c-92d9-d73b49291025", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Score analysis", "children": [{"id": "56d9bdde-fa9c-43db-a701-86cd3562c0ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Roman numerals"}, {"id": "724bd8ab-8643-4d5f-9a47-9b539033abfd", "type": "concept", "title": "formal location"}, {"id": "3027ddf2-9a07-4fea-839d-f5438dee5135", "type": "concept", "title": "voice-leading evidence"}], "description": "Students identify chromatic devices and explain their local and large-scale roles."}, {"id": "a53bf3fb-1d3a-4d59-b374-1b814f12d2c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Listening and performance meaning", "children": [{"id": "b2457815-7fc2-4e7d-b149-42019346e0a6", "type": "concept", "title": "expressive dissonance"}, {"id": "348bdb9b-bd76-4895-bc30-ee0ef0524535", "type": "concept", "title": "arrival shaping"}, {"id": "0daba9b0-ad2d-4caa-a545-562b78b0e571", "type": "concept", "title": "phrase intensity"}], "description": "The course connects chromatic harmony to tension, color, pacing, and interpretation."}, {"id": "aba3112d-a37c-428c-92b7-608fd2e26436", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical and stylistic context", "children": [{"id": "df8da076-ee41-4d5a-be1c-fdb1239466f3", "type": "concept", "title": "common-practice syntax"}, {"id": "1591b392-c98e-4ff9-bb48-1f79f52bffb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Romantic color"}, {"id": "1456198b-6ded-4d24-8498-078df779bf86", "type": "concept", "title": "screen harmony"}], "description": "Students place chromatic techniques in classical, Romantic, popular, and film-music settings."}]}, {"id": "6fb214c8-2f35-4712-bc98-4754389da9b7", "type": "topic", "title": "Aural, Keyboard, and Composition Integration", "description": "This added world-class unit makes chromatic theory practical by requiring students to hear, play, and write the concepts they analyze.", "children": [{"id": "a992c99d-7935-47f7-bc4c-4d74b266eefc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aural recognition", "children": [{"id": "9147c5f7-8a6a-408f-a670-3b6ab455c5dc", "type": "concept", "title": "secondary dominant hearing"}, {"id": "ebd0d8cc-cc00-4556-a0c2-4b8de6659ceb", "type": "concept", "title": "mixture color"}, {"id": "12ce8026-04d5-42f3-873c-6144af995e91", "type": "concept", "title": "modulation tracking"}], "description": "Students learn to hear applied dominants, mixture, modulation, and augmented-sixth sonorities."}, {"id": "e8c76023-ee68-4b22-bb89-e60c625e2f2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Keyboard realization", "children": [{"id": "912afa8c-ca69-4ff5-b1fc-4188997b8395", "type": "concept", "title": "applied dominant chains"}, {"id": "2b5b98b0-8b9b-49f2-8df9-9141eb3ed019", "type": "concept", "title": "Neapolitan to V"}, {"id": "aede2235-bcfa-4cf5-84da-1ab8dfffff02", "type": "concept", "title": "augmented sixth to V"}], "description": "Students play chromatic progressions to internalize sound and voice leading."}, {"id": "e7e986fc-76c9-4e03-9f35-93da17fe4995", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Short composition tasks", "children": [{"id": "536de6cd-1084-4fd2-a73c-8ad24016036d", "type": "concept", "title": "modulating period"}, {"id": "123a057b-a7f2-485c-b3cb-5059c52eb8b4", "type": "concept", "title": "mixture progression"}, {"id": "974b9505-9c85-40eb-a8fd-78c5598d7496", "type": "concept", "title": "chromatic predominant phrase"}], "description": "Students compose phrase models using chromatic devices and clear formal goals."}]}, {"id": "1266a39a-964b-4b89-8f0b-0563a5f8d600", "type": "topic", "title": "Analytical Writing and Cross-Genre Application", "description": "This added capstone asks students to explain chromatic harmony clearly and connect it to broader musical practice.", "children": [{"id": 