onal ambiguity"}], "description": "Students connect these techniques to expanded tonal palettes."}]}, {"id": "faea0044-0169-4f7f-b3e0-1ddda504b3b2", "type": "topic", "title": "Chromatic Harmony in Context", "description": "Students synthesize chromatic harmony through repertoire, listening, and stylistic interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "030aae08-94e2-468c-92d9-d73b49291025", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Score analysis", "children": [{"id": "56d9bdde-fa9c-43db-a701-86cd3562c0ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Roman numerals"}, {"id": "724bd8ab-8643-4d5f-9a47-9b539033abfd", "type": "concept", "title": "formal location"}, {"id": "3027ddf2-9a07-4fea-839d-f5438dee5135", "type": "concept", "title": "voice-leading evidence"}], "description": "Students identify chromatic devices and explain their local and large-scale roles."}, {"id": "a53bf3fb-1d3a-4d59-b374-1b814f12d2c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Listening and performance meaning", "children": [{"id": "b2457815-7fc2-4e7d-b149-42019346e0a6", "type": "concept", "title": "expressive dissonance"}, {"id": "348bdb9b-bd76-4895-bc30-ee0ef0524535", "type": "concept", "title": "arrival shaping"}, {"id": "0daba9b0-ad2d-4caa-a545-562b78b0e571", "type": "concept", "title": "phrase intensity"}], "description": "The course connects chromatic harmony to tension, color, pacing, and interpretation."}, {"id": "aba3112d-a37c-428c-92b7-608fd2e26436", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical and stylistic context", "children": [{"id": "df8da076-ee41-4d5a-be1c-fdb1239466f3", "type": "concept", "title": "common-practice syntax"}, {"id": "1591b392-c98e-4ff9-bb48-1f79f52bffb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Romantic color"}, {"id": "1456198b-6ded-4d24-8498-078df779bf86", "type": "concept", "title": "screen harmony"}], "description": "Students place chromatic techniques in classical, Romantic, popular, and film-music settings."}]}, {"id": "6fb214c8-2f35-4712-bc98-4754389da9b7", "type": "topic", "title": "Aural, Keyboard, and Composition I